o-products, as well as merchandises and trades in other biofuels, such as renewable feedstocks. The Andersons, Inc. was founded in 1947 and is based in Maumee, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William E. Krueger | CEO, President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $5.4M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["The Andersons, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $1.9B market cap on $11.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +114% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 7% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $56M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 219% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.1949107930997083},{"tex